From: =?UTF-8?q?Trung=20L=C3=AA?= <8@tle.id.au>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:33:31 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Add a PPC64 backend
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A JIT for ppc64le hosts and the Power ISA paths and emulation fixes that
go with it, squashed from the 13 commits of
https://github.com/runlevel5/dolphin-ppc64/pull/1:

- Add a JIT for ppc64le hosts
- VideoCommon: process the FIFO in batches on the GPU thread
- JitPPC64: fix a sign-compare warning in IsReadAgainAsSingles
- VideoCommon: run async requests in FIFO order on the GPU thread
- Core: run the clock at host pace on idle while the GPU thread is busy
- JitPPC64: compile quantized accesses for the GQR's value even when it changes
- VideoCommon: have a CP register access wait for the GPU thread to fetch
- JitPPC64: translate page table accesses in the access's far code
- JitPPC64: access what a DBAT maps through the physical arena
- MMU: after a tlbie, look at the PTEs for its page only
- JitPPC64: test for the non-IEEE flush where the value is
- VideoCommon: wake the GPU thread for a burst only when it can take it
- VideoCommon: load vertex attributes with VSX on Power ISA 3.0

The individual commits, with their rationale and measurements, are in that
pull request.

